1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:06,680
Let's go.

2
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:07,160
Come on.

3
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,000
Let's get a massage.

4
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:10,840
I'm really curious about your paintings.

5
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,880
Would that be considered
gongbi painting?

6
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:13,640
I don't know.

7
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:14,200
I was just guessing.

8
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:14,880
Gongbi...

9
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,000
The linework

10
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,960
is more in the gongbi style.

11
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,400
And I also do

12
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,040
mineral pigment painting.

13
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,160
I paint thangkas too.

14
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,260
Wow.

15
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,080
You can do everything.

16
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:30,640
We're stuck in traffic.

17
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:35,040
Every time Cao Yiheng
makes eye contact with me,

18
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:35,680
I want to laugh.

19
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:36,440
Why?

20
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,360
At first, I never really saw you

21
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,600
laugh your heart out.

22
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,040
Except for these two times.

23
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,120
Once was when I took

24
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,160
that hilarious photo of you.

25
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,640
I'm over here practicing my poses...

26
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:47,760
He turns into a supermodel.

27
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,160
These are both me.

28
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,480
Too handsome for the camera.

29
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:54,880
Okay.

30
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:56,200
Yeah.

31
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,320
And the other time was just now.

32
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,040
I think your laugh

33
00:00:58,040 --> 00:00:59,200
is pretty contagious too.

34
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:01,960
Like I said at first,

35
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:03,760
once you get to know me,

36
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:05,000
I'm actually pretty goofy.

37
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,160
I can tell.

38
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,080
Yeah.

39
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,560
Let's go.

40
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:20,560
Wow.

41
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:21,880
What a spread.

42
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:22,520
Okay.

43
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,120
I'll start with...

44
00:01:23,120 --> 00:01:24,000
Is this amount okay?

45
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:24,920
Yeah.

46
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,680
Do you think

47
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,880
the "kite-type lover"

48
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,720
description

49
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,680
fits you?

50
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,680
I think...

51
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,840
I'd say I lean more

52
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:39,880
toward it.

53
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:42,600
If I asked you guys

54
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:43,120
the question

55
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:43,760
I got yesterday,

56
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:44,320
what would you say?

57
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:45,000
Like,

58
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,920
how would you balance

59
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:47,960
work and a relationship?

60
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:50,280
Basically, outside of work,

61
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:51,360
it's all about relationships.

62
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:00,760
What about you, Liang Xiaoyu?

63
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,480
I feel like...

64
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:08,120
a relationship

65
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,600
can be a source of comfort

66
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:10,480
outside of work.

67
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,440
Especially when

68
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:17,040
work gets exhausting,

69
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,240
you realize

70
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:20,520
just how important

71
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,480
a relationship can be

72
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:23,400
and how irreplaceable it is.

73
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,240
I think when we talk

74
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,560
about balance,

75
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:30,360
we have to consider

76
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,960
how much time we spend

77
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:32,840
and how much energy

78
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:34,960
we put into it.

79
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:35,640
Right.

80
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,600
Work will naturally

81
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,080
take up more of our time.

82
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:39,240
Exactly.

83
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:43,040
We may not spend as much time

84
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:44,400
on a relationship,

85
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,560
but we might put more emotional energy

86
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,560
into it.

87
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:52,280
That's true.

88
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,240
That makes a lot of sense.

89
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:55,200
Cao Yiheng still hasn't

90
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,360
answered my question.

91
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:59,160
I actually agree

92
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:01,400
with what Liang Xiaoyu just said.

93
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,840
You two are on the same page.

94
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:03,720
You really agree?

95
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:05,000
Yeah, because...

96
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:06,880
Work already takes up

97
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,560
most of the day.

98
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:09,120
So you can't really

99
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,000
compare the two.

100
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:10,720
You just can't.

101
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:12,240
They're not on the same scale.

102
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,400
One is about actual time,

103
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,640
while the other is about how you feel.

104
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:16,960
That makes sense.

105
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:20,040
So when Chen Hewen talked about it,

106
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,680
did he literally mean
splitting his time?

107
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:22,520
Yeah, just time.

108
00:03:22,520 --> 00:03:23,480
I think

109
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,600
work used to take up

110
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,720
most of my life.

111
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:27,800
But if I had

112
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,560
a partner,

113
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:29,600
I'd probably divide

114
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,800
my time more evenly.

115
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:33,200
Working hard

116
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:34,840
would also give us

117
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,040
a better life together.

118
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:37,120
I think that's

119
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,560
really important.

120
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:42,160
But aren't you already really busy?

121
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:42,640
I am.

122
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,000
If you start making time

123
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,880
for a relationship,

124
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,000
you'll only have half
as much time for work.

125
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,240
I think I can manage.

126
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,680
So are you two

127
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,960
going to stay

128
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:55,880
long-distance?

129
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:57,640
She's studying in Beijing,

130
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,520
and I work in Tianjin.

131
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,600
But it's really not that far.

132
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,640
So I guess that means

133
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:04,080
you come to Beijing a lot?

134
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,240
That's nice.

135
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:12,040
So have you thought about

136
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,440
what you want

137
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:14,400
for the future?

138
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:14,720
Any plans

139
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,160
or things you're looking forward to?

140
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,800
For the next

141
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,880
three or four years,

142
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,880
we plan to keep doing...

143
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:23,920
what we're doing now.

144
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,600
That's the plan for now.

145
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,800
So she'll focus on school,

146
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:30,280
and you'll focus on work.

147
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,840
Then whenever you're both free,
you can meet up.

148
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:32,800
She can go back to Tianjin,

149
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,920
or you can come to Beijing.

150
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,280
Yeah.

151
00:04:35,280 --> 00:04:36,360
You two seem really happy.

152
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,840
Let's have a toast.

153
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:41,640
Cheers.

154
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:43,920
Did I somehow turn this

155
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,440
into a serious

156
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,040
conversation?

157
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:55,560
We're home.

158
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,200
I'm hungry.

159
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,840
We're all hungry.

160
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:07,680
Let's grab something to eat.

161
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,320
Okay.

162
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:09,520
Let's go get some.

163
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,720
Give me the bag.

164
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,640
I'll leave my stuff here.

165
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,640
Straight to the food.

166
00:05:21,620 --> 00:05:22,340
(Gesturing)

167
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,040
What?

168
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,440
Is there something on me?

169
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:26,760
No, don't move.

170
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:27,700
(Leans closer)

171
00:05:29,860 --> 00:05:31,300
(Focused)

172
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:32,480
Okay.

173
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:33,440
Lipstick.

174
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:36,440
What's with your hair?

175
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:37,680
Why does it look so light?

176
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:40,160
Is the color different
on the top and bottom?

177
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,240
Do you like yesterday's hair

178
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,120
or today's?

179
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:45,600
Hard to say.

180
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,800
They're different styles.

181
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,280
You like both.

182
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:50,640
I think both look pretty good.

183
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,280
Super confident.

184
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:52,860
(Teasing)

185
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,760
No, I think both look great.

186
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:56,440
(Backtracking)
Yeah.

187
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,360
What did you mean?

188
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,180
They both look good.

189
00:05:58,180 --> 00:05:59,320
You called me super confident.

190
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,340
(Stares)

191
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,720
No.

192
00:06:02,720 --> 00:06:03,840
Confidence is a good thing. Really.

193
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:05,540
(Nods)

194
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,120
Want some of this?

195
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:08,760
Let me help.

196
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:12,320
Give it to me.

197
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:13,240
It's kinda prickly.

198
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,200
Let's make an egg pancake.

199
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:16,960
Sure.

200
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:17,360
Sound good?

201
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,120
Yeah, sure.

202
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:19,920
I'm seriously starving.

203
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,200
I'm starving as well.

204
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:21,880
Same here.

205
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:23,560
You guys want some?

206
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,480
Want some eggs?

207
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:26,220
(Offering)

208
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:27,120
Sure.

209
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,120
Okay.

210
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:29,080
Boiled eggs.

211
00:06:29,080 --> 00:06:30,260
I'll go take a look.

212
00:06:30,260 --> 00:06:30,900
See what they've got.

213
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:31,680
Let's take a look.

214
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:33,440
See what's there.

215
00:06:36,820 --> 00:06:38,540
(Eggs boiled by Yu Yang)

216
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,240
Now we're talking.

217
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:41,960
I boiled eight.

218
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:43,400
Eight?

219
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,440
Eight eggs?

220
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:48,040
What would

221
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,400
taste good with eggs?

222
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,760
This should go well with this.

223
00:06:53,760 --> 00:06:55,280
Let's use this.

224
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:57,240
We made our own little combo.

225
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:58,580
(Feeds her)

226
00:07:06,140 --> 00:07:07,380
(Hands it over)

227
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,440
It's actually pretty good.

228
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:16,800
Is it too sweet?

229
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:17,600
Not really.

230
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,560
Here, use this knife.

231
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,640
Want some jam?

232
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:22,520
Thanks.

233
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
Thanks.

234
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:35,240
Hey, guys.

235
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,200
Hello!

236
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,400
You're back.

237
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,160
We brought food back.

238
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:43,980
(Local food just for them)
Wow!

239
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,160
You guys came back together?

240
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,160
(Leaves)
Let's go play some pool.

241
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,000
I'm heading back.

242
00:07:59,120 --> 00:07:59,960
How's this table?

243
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:01,360
Better than the other one?

244
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,440
About the same.

245
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:04,920
Should we take this

246
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:06,040
to the table and eat?

247
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:06,920
Sure.

248
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,640
Give it to me.

249
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,120
There are chopsticks here.

250
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:25,400
And forks.

251
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:26,440
Thanks.

252
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:27,960
I'll use a fork.

253
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,240
I prefer forks.

254
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,240
Same here.

255
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:30,840
I like forks.

256
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:33,640
You take it.

257
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:34,240
Give it to me.

258
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,240
Fight it out.

259
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:35,920
No.

260
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,180
(Behave)

261
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,080
Sorry.

262
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:42,720
Do you always have carbs
with every meal?

263
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:44,920
Not really. I usually eat more veggies.

264
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:45,800
You gotta have some.

265
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,200
Thanks.

266
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:52,880
Did you eat this?

267
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,880
(Serves her some)
Yeah, I did.

268
00:08:53,890 --> 00:08:54,880
Have one.

269
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,240
Here, eat this.

270
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,080
Are you coming back out later?

271
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,320
Nope.

272
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:01,660
(Teasing)

273
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:02,880
I will.

274
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,720
Just kidding.

275
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:12,040
Your sleeve.

276
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,600
This is pretty good.

277
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:14,920
Wait, your...

278
00:09:16,900 --> 00:09:18,500
(Fixes her sleeve)

279
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:22,940
(Smiles)

280
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:41,160
Cui Yihang, how was the elephant camp?

281
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,120
Did you get to ride the elephants or...

282
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:43,880
Give them a bath?

283
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:44,840
How should I put this?

284
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:47,040
We helped deliver a baby elephant.

285
00:09:47,040 --> 00:09:48,280
What? Deliver one?

286
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:49,480
Yeah, we helped with the birth.

287
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:50,880
We actually saw it happen.

288
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,240
Seriously?

289
00:09:52,540 --> 00:09:53,440
(Glances)

290
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,680
A baby elephant was born.

291
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:55,420
(Plays along)

292
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,120
Aren't there black elephants too?

293
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,040
They come in all kinds of colors.

294
00:09:58,440 --> 00:09:59,400
There's also...

295
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:00,520
There's also a pink elephant.

296
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,000
Yeah, newborns are pink.

297
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:02,960
What about yellow ones?

298
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:03,920
No yellow ones.

299
00:10:03,920 --> 00:10:05,480
Just pinkish.

300
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:06,740
Have you been hanging out

301
00:10:06,740 --> 00:10:07,640
with Cui Yihang too much?

